; The default chunking decision measures the stream bytes that became code:
; the reader's bytes minus the bytes of the bodies lazy emission dropped
; (project.md decision 14).  The stream of lazy-basic.test has two dropped
; bodies, so the lazy run counts fewer body bytes than the stream has, and the
; eager run (--eager-bodies, nothing dropped) counts all of them.  The two
; stats outputs go to one FileCheck: the eager `chunk decision` line repeats the
; stream's byte count, the lazy one must not.  (Without the subtraction the
; lazy run would report the stream's bytes too.)  The threshold between the
; two counts is lazy-chunk-bytes-hook.test.
; RUN: cat %S/Inputs/header11_supp.txt %S/lazy-basic.test > %t.txt
; RUN: %ecil-asm %t.txt -o %t.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --eager-bodies --stats --emit=llvm -o %t.e.ll %t.ecil 2> %t.err
; RUN: %edg-cir --stats --emit=llvm -o %t.l.ll %t.ecil 2>> %t.err
; RUN: %FileCheck %s < %t.err

; CHECK: stats: {{.*}} frames, {{.*}} records, [[TOTAL:[0-9]+]] bytes
; CHECK: stats: chunk decision: [[TOTAL]] body bytes, threshold 1250000{{$}}
; CHECK: stats: {{.*}} frames, {{.*}} records, [[TOTAL]] bytes
; The lazy run's decision line is the rest of the file (a CHECK-NOT that is
; followed by a positive check would not see the line that check matches); that
; it exists and its number are in lazy-chunk-bytes-hook.test.
; CHECK-NOT: stats: chunk decision: [[TOTAL]] body bytes
